Venetium 0012 - X86-1 build fixes: three patched sources that did not compile in the first x86 build (BATCH-X86-1 section 1.5).

A. components/url_formatter/url_fixer.cc - Supermium's general_features.patch calls base::CommandLine (the
   omnibox-autocomplete-filtering check) but the file never includes base/command_line.h; in Chromium 150 only a forward
   declaration reaches it ("incomplete type 'base::CommandLine'"). Fix: #include "base/command_line.h".

B. components/translate/core/browser/translate_ranker_impl.cc - Venetium 0007 (ungoogled-chromium's
   toggle-translation-via-switch) puts a bare `return kDefaultResponse;` at the top of ShouldOfferTranslation(), so the
   rest of the function is unreachable; Chromium builds its own code with -Wunreachable-code-aggressive and warnings as
   errors. Fix: return before anything is recorded when the ranker is neither queried nor enforced - always true, since
   0007 sets both to false in the constructor. Same behaviour, no dead code.

C. chrome/browser/supermium_flag_choices.h, supermium_flag_entries.h (new) - Supermium's
   150_about_flags_and_finishing_touches.patch includes them in about_flags.cc, but no Supermium patch creates them
   (VENETIUM-1 finding 4). Supermium's main (v150 patch set, also as revised 2026-09-30) has neither file; its branch v144
   (82756ad4) has both (git blobs 1452f912, 9a183cc7; fork lll69/supermium patch-touchscreen-150.0.7871.253 holds the same
   blobs). Taken from v144 and adapted to Supermium's 150 patches, keeping Supermium's text and order:
   - 4 entries whose feature the 150 patches replaced by a switch now set that switch: clear-data-on-exit,
     disable-qr-generator, top-chrome-toasts -> disable-toasts, show-managed-ui -> disable-managed-ui;
   - 2 entries whose feature no longer exists are left out: download-bubble, power-bookmarks-side-panel;
   - 12 entries whose switch nothing in the 150 tree reads are left out: force-gdi, bookmark-bar-ntp, remove-grab-handle,
     disable-grease-tls, hide-sidepanel-button, override-tab-outline-default, override-new-tab-button-shape-default,
     legacy-tooltips-win, max-connections-per-host, native-ui-style, old-tab-strip-bounds, disable-crashpad; with them the
     2 choice arrays only they used (kBookmarkBarNewTab, kMaxConnectionsPerHostChoices);
   - ungoogled-supermium is kept: chrome_browser_main.cc enables it by name; its switch's reader is in Supermium's
     2026-09-30 ungoogled_supermium_and_mv2.patch, which this tree does not have yet.
   Result: 51 of 65 entries, 8 of 10 choice arrays. The duplicate internal name windows11-mica-titlebar (Supermium's
   switch entry and upstream's feature entry) is kept as Supermium has it.

Made by BATCH-X86-1 after section 1.8 (his decision, 2026-10-01: fix here; fetch the headers if Supermium or a fork has
them, else write them). Proof: the three objects compile; s9/state-0012.sha256; round trip of 0001..0012.

